      "title": "Setup and model downloads",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MLX text-guided keying\n\n1. Download the tested MIT-licensed [Florence-2 base fine-tune Q8 MLX bundle](https://huggingface.co/mlx-community/Florence-2-base-ft-8bit). Keep the complete bundle in `ComfyUI/models/florence2/Florence-2-base-ft-8bit/`. The older Q4 conversion is not supported because its coordinate tokens are unreliable.\n2. Install the separately licensed [CorridorKey MLX runtime](https://github.com/nikopueringer/corridorkey-mlx), review its [license](https://github.com/nikopueringer/CorridorKey/blob/main/LICENSE), and put its [MLX checkpoint](https://github.com/nikopueringer/corridorkey-mlx/releases/tag/v1.0.0) in `ComfyUI/models/corridorkey/`.\n3. Select source footage in **Load Image** and describe one foreground subject in **Florence-2 Text Auto Mask**. The image field is intentionally empty.\n4. The default evaluates Florence every eight frames plus the final frame, interpolates the grounded location, refines a subject silhouette, unloads Florence, then runs CorridorKey. Set the stride to `1` for maximum tracking accuracy.\n5. Queue the workflow. Review the green silhouette before trusting the final checkerboard preview. The orange rectangle shows the Florence search region. For difficult motion, use a smaller stride or another standard ComfyUI `MASK` provider."
      ],
      "color": "#243447",
      "bgcolor": "#15202b"
    }
